w('# Issue 33 — remeasurement after the #37 polarity fix');w();w('**Research recommendation: no automatic recolouring change is warranted on this evidence.** The strongest surviving edge mismatch is on financial mixed lines; it is not a universal property of all documents. Any owner-authorised follow-up should first demonstrate source-faithful, legible characters and improvements on paired, held-out lines at reading size, including historical print, without forcing black or compromising counters, punctuation or extraction. This study changes no product code. Independent review by Claude is pending.')
w();w('## Baseline and scope');w();w('Main `ab7dfba96561595e7c587d8033954ed1ec235a20` was built with `cargo build --release --locked -p scanweave-cli` and converted at `--dpi 300 --profile clearscan --glyph-sharing off`. All five completed PDFs match the frozen #39 C-prime outputs. [provenance.json](provenance.json) includes the input, Adobe XI, old and corrected PDF hashes. All 32 pages have identical parsed OCR text and boxes in the old and new reports; raw hOCR hashes differ, while the parsed text and boxes used for these measurements match ([OCR provenance](ocr-provenance.json)).')
w();w('| Document | Corrected PDF SHA-256 | Bytes |');w('|---|---|---:|')
